      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The wealth gap in the US is primarily due to a combination of policies favoring the wealthy, such as tax cuts for the rich, deregulation, and the decline of unions. These policies have disproportionately benefited the upper class, while the middle and lower classes have seen stagnant wages and limited social mobility. Additionally, the increasing influence of money in politics has led to legislation that further entrenches these disparities. The root cause is a system that prioritizes the interests of the wealthy over the needs of the majority.",
      "source": "target",
